; example-a.test - rendered by gen_lab.py into generated/dns: the serial, the
; address of moved and the intra record are filled in there. Not DNSSEC-signed.
;
; TTL and negative TTL are 1 s: systemd-resolved on the host caches by TTL, and a
; cached answer never reaches CoreDNS's query log, so a "0 PTR queries" check
; would pass on a cache hit. With 1 s nothing survives from one run to the next.
$ORIGIN example-a.test.
$TTL 1
@        IN SOA ns1.example-a.test. hostmaster.example-a.test. @SERIAL@ 3600 600 86400 1
@        IN NS  ns1.example-a.test.
ns1      IN A   192.88.98.53

; .10's SNI vhosts. web and app are also .10's two PTR names.
web      IN A   192.88.98.10
app      IN A   192.88.98.10
; Only the urlscan stub (.30) names it: not in any certificate, no PTR.
hidden   IN A   192.88.98.10
; Swapped between .10 and .99 by set_moved.sh (E8, E21).
moved    IN A   @MOVED_IP@

; Resolves to a target AND the outsider: never scannable by name.
split    IN A   192.88.98.13
split    IN A   192.88.98.99

; Behind the CDN-like edge.
cdn1     IN A   192.88.98.40

; Only the urlscan stub names it, and it points at the outsider.
gone     IN A   192.88.98.99

; nodns: in .10's default certificate and deliberately without any record.
; *.wild: a wildcard SAN in .10's default certificate, deliberately without records.

@INTRA_RECORD@
